  "raw_text": "Step 1: Determine the total number of possible outcomes.\nThe numbers range from 1 to 100, so there are 100 possible outcomes.\n\nStep 2: Identify how many numbers between 1 and 100 are multiples of 3.\nTo find this, we divide 100 by 3 and take the integer part of the quotient.\n100 ÷ 3 = 33 remainder 1, so there are 33 multiples of 3 within this range.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the probability.\nProbability = (Number of favorable outcomes) / (Total number of possible outcomes)\nProbability = 33 / 100\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{33/100}<|im_end|>",
